    "summary": "The drummer who turned jazz time into a rolling, polyrhythmic wave. In John Coltrane's classic quartet he layered independent metres across hands and feet, so the drummer became a co-improviser with the soloist rather than a timekeeper. His triplet-saturated swing reshaped jazz drumming and crossed into rock through Ginger Baker and Mitch Mitchell."
  },
